    rationale: "California establishes a base year value generally on a change in ownership, with annual increases limited thereafter — which is exactly why a buyer's property tax will not be the seller's. The correct statement quotes the seller's bill as the seller's, explains the coming reassessment, and routes the estimate to the assessor and a tax professional.",
